WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.480
Taiwan

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.110
You called, sir?

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:11.800
Kaoruko, I have news on 
your father's whereabouts.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.410
We've learned that he's currently 
at the Buranki nest.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.960
What? How did he get there?

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.550
It's nothing less than shocking,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:24.460
but it turns out there are still Buranki 
on Earth whose brains haven't died.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.770
Your father borrowed the power of one

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.550
to go up to the Buranki 
nest and open the gate.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.890
So you're saying he got in a Buranki 
that had no contract with a human

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.780
and went to Treasure Island in it?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.890
Precisely.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:42.270
A Buranki with a functioning brain 
could open the gate with no problem.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.760
That's way beyond anything I imagined.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.730
Typical Dad. I guess I should've 
expected that from him.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:54.570
Though it's still unclear how he 
negotiated with a conscious Buranki.

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.940
Knowing my dad, he probably 
had a few drinks with it.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.460
And so the two lovers 
found one another again.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.350
How truly lovely.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.710
They're the textbook married couple.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.160
Marriage is the oldest and most 
sacred of all the contracts

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.470
two people can exchange.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.020
Do you want to see your parents?

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:19.970
Not really!

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.640
Kaoruko, there is a way to see your parents.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.180
Just bring them down here to Earth.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.160
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.160
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.180
BURANKI

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.850
BURANKI

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:09.650
BURANKI

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.540
Kazuki

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.540
Kaoruko

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.450
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:00.450
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.950
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.950
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.100
Th-This is...

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.040
What?

00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:14.000
Well, this is the result of our analysis...

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.880
And it looks like Entei has a brain— no,

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:20.470
something resembling nerve 
tissue, acting as a brain.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.340
What does that mean?

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:27.440
Doesn't Entei need a human because 
its brain has already died?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.850
If that's true...

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:32.790
How were Reoko and Kaoruko 
able to control Entei?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:37.570
I don't have a clear answer 
for that at the moment.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:42.610
For us to fully control Entei henceforth

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.060
will require the elimination 
of uncertainties.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.480
You understand that, yes?

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:47.580
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:50.200
If I can have just a bit 
more time to do that...

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.360
Time, eh...

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.110
I hear this place was 
once an execution site.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.090
Did you know that?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.460
Yes. It's pretty creepy, isn't it?

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:06.310
Perhaps that's why several people 
still go missing here each year.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:12.060
What's more, it seems that only 
incompetent engineers disappear.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.150
Well, get back to work. And show me results!

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.560
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.200
<b>Sealed</b>

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:38.840
Just bring them down here to Earth.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:41.230
Is that possible?

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:44.820
Not in one leap, but if 
we give them steps, yes.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.850
First, I need you to guide your 
brother to the Buranki nest.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.100
Azuma? Why him?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:55.180
Since he has the heart of 
Oubu, the only Buranki

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.860
on Earth besides Entei that 
can still function on Earth,

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.320
I need him to enter Oubu's cranium and

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.780
open the gate to the Buranki nest.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.030
If that's what you need done, I'll do it!

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:10.410
How? You don't have a Buranki 
heart, let alone a Buranki.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:15.450
Once the gate is open, the rest is easy.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.290
Maxim and his team will 
bring it down from the sky.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.710
Bring it down? You mean Treasure Island?

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.920
My parents won't be hurt 
if you do that, will they?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.490
Of course they won't.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:30.100
Breaking the barrier around that 
island would be far more difficult.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:33.430
All right.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:36.880
And I'll really be able 
to see my mom and dad?

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:47.030
I swear it on my life.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.040
Are you awake?

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:04.130
I like that look in your eyes!
You are gutsy, indeed!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.830
As I'd expect of Kazuki Migiwa's daughter.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.640
You're going to pilot Entei one more time.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.940
And you're going to kill 
every last Bubuki user.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:24.210
Keep killing and killing until you 
lose track of the body count,

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.670
and you're sure to become a hero.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.580
Just as mass murderers throughout

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:31.300
history have come to be known as heroes.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:33.660
You scum!

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.260
What are you gonna do?!

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.340
No! No! Stop it!

00:06:52.980 --> 00:06:56.190
Daughter of the witch, with her 
loathsome blood in your veins...

00:06:57.690 --> 00:07:01.310
I've created a fitting role just for you.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:09.740
Long story short,

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.320
it should be possible

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:14.750
to fuse Kaoruko's brain with the 
nerve tissue in Entei's cranium

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:18.410
and control it from the outside.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.910
So you're saying as long as we 
have Kaoruko from the neck up,

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:25.040
we can control Entei.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:29.280
Yes, provided that the bonding 
of the severed head to Entei

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:32.550
is carried out with utmost 
speed and precision.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:38.770
Then cut off Kaoruko's head with the giant 
sickle the Russian kids left behind.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:45.600
I selected you as my most trusted 
aide in spite of much opposition.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.170
I'd like to see results from 
you that justify my choice.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.860
I will not fail to live 
up to your expectations.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.560
We will exterminate every
Buranki user and their bloodline,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.790
and wipe all Buranki 
from the face of the earth.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.420
We must restore ownership 
of this world to humans.

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:19.890
Reoko-sama's weakness may be a result

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:23.170
of her separation from Entei.

00:08:23.170 --> 00:08:28.900
So it's only Entei's power 
that keeps her body going?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.340
Azuma...

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.900
Shh.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:39.340
Sorry, Azuma.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.660
Reoko-sama is asking for you.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.680
Well, we'll leave the rest to you.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:36.360
Your father was a tough man.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:40.610
He probably never gave much 
thought to his own health.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:46.730
After he came back here, I could 
only spend a short time with him.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:50.220
I wonder if your father was happy.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.650
I hope he was.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:02.000
He got to be with you in the end.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:05.160
I know he was happy.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.980
<b>Episode 18
The Butterfly
and the Gallows</b>

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.980
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI
The Gentle Giants
 of the Galaxy</i></b>

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:37.490
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI</i></b>

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.490
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.410
You should be laughing at the 
shape I'm in, son of Migiwa.

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:50.870
When separated from Entei, 
I am so powerless.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.840
I am only keeping myself alive

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:57.430
by acting as Entei's heart.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:59.880
How pathetic.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:03.370
And I'm supposed to stop Guy?

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:06.310
What is this Guy person trying to do?

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:11.690
He wants to resurrect the 
Buranki's progenitor.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:14.450
That's what he told me.

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:16.970
Their progenitor?

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:20.700
Guy called it the Buranki "Deus Magna."

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.460
He said it was essentially 
the god of Buranki,

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.770
who gave life to all Buranki on Earth.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:30.710
Guy hopes to use it to rebuild this world.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.240
It's said that the 
resurrection of Deus Magna

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.250
can be brought about using that 
comet and the Buranki nest.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.590
Comet?

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.350
How can that comet and Treasure Island...?

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.600
I don't know.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:50.230
In any case, we have little time remaining.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:54.610
Guy said the comet will 
fall in only seven days.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.900
That soon?!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.510
That is why we must find the Buranki nest

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:01.110
that sank into the sea before Guy does.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:04.100
What do we do once we find it?

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:08.490
Crush it to dust and bury it so Guy 
can't use it for his own purposes.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:10.200
That is the only way.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.130
Hey, Tsuwabuki...

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:21.860
Is all of this part of the land you bought?

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:25.140
Yes. I learned this afterward,

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:30.500
but apparently the mansion of Guy Barville 
Abeille, president of Demokratia,

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.230
is just over that hill.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:36.380
What?! The enemy's supreme 
commander is right next door?!

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:38.730
Yes, in a remarkable coincidence.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.070
Coincidence? Are you serious?

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:44.150
"It's darkest at the foot of the 
lighthouse." We'll be fine, I'm sure.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.610
Yeah, but...

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:50.230
You've gotten to be quite 
the worrywart, Shuusaku.

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:52.060
Do people really change this much

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.380
when they suddenly have 
something to protect?

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.420
I-It's not that.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.540
Anyway...

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:04.400
What the hell could Reoko-sama 
want to talk to Azuma about?

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.220
You once told me

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:13.130
that Migiwa tried to protect the 
lives of both Buranki and humans.

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:15.320
But you should face reality.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:19.730
The Buranki nest has fallen and 
is about to be used by Guy.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.740
Yeah, that's how it turned out.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:27.370
I couldn't protect anything.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:31.190
Not my mom, Treasure Island, or Kaoruko.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:33.750
If you have power, you can protect anything.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.410
That is what I've always done.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:39.750
All you talk about is power!
That's why we're constantly at war!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.210
You have it backwards.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.710
Use power to instill fear 
and control others.

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.760
Then war won't happen.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.450
Why don't we step outside for a bit?

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.120
<b>Cup Noodles</b>

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:16.400
Don't be shy! There's plenty to go around!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:20.670
We come all the way to France, 
and we have to eat cup noodles?!

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.380
It's not to your tastes?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.450
We can't even drink alcohol!

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.420
But this is my best bottle!

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.020
I seriously can't believe this!

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:28.730
Yeah, yeah!

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:31.530
Men around forty who can't even cook 
or do anything to support themselves!

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.470
Yeah, yeah!

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:35.340
I see nothing but loneliness 
in their future!

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:37.100
They'll probably end up divorced, too!

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:42.190
<b>Censored</b>

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:42.230
I can just see a white-haired Matobai 
trying to wash his own underwear!

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:43.360
So sad!

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.370
And Tsuwabuki all alone and bedridden 
in a trash-filled house!

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:48.650
<b>Censored</b>

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.650
No future!

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.810
Forget it.

00:14:52.810 --> 00:14:55.430
Let's leave these useless geezers 
and do this on our own, Kogane!

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:57.040
Got it, Kino-chan!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.330
Hey, what the heck?
There's nothing good in here.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.840
Hey, Kino-chan, what's French miso like?

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:06.400
Dunno... I wonder.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.340
Left behind...

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:17.060
I saw a butterfly near the window earlier.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.820
That species of butterfly 
isn't native to France.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.310
Where did it come from?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.480
A butterfly?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:35.960
So the user of Oubu's heart,
who stood before me and Entei in battle,

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:39.420
turns out to be a child 
who loves bug-hunting?

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.690
For goodness' sake.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:44.830
You said earlier that if you use power 
to instill fear and control people,

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:47.020
war would never occur, right?

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:48.630
What of it?

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:52.130
Then can you control bugs with fear, too?

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.890
Don't compare humans to bugs.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:59.550
Are your eyes only able to see humans now?

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:04.150
But there are so many other 
living things all around us.

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.380
Are you trying to lecture me?

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:15.910
Before, Akihito said that he'd 
taken up gardening as a diversion.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:18.070
Was he talking about this place?

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:21.280
Dirt...

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:31.630
How long has it been since I touched it?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.740
Perhaps...

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.870
I really have only seen 
humans for all this time.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:15.720
"'I don't want to lose my head,' Karen said.

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:21.680
'Then I won't be able to repent of my sins.'

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:27.480
'But please, cut off my feet 
along with these red shoes.'"

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.120
Scary...

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:31.940
All right, everyone, that's all for today.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.780
Aw!

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:44.390
Goodnight, children. Sweet dreams.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:09.730
You're going to save Kaoruko-chan, right?

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:10.810
Kogane-chan...

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.040
Of course you are.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:16.700
It only makes sense for the older 
brother to save his little sister.

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:18.470
But...

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:21.790
I wish you had told me.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:22.700
Sorry.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:26.590
I told you not to try so hard by yourself!

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:30.000
When there's something I can do,
come to me for help!

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.370
Kogane-chan...

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.990
Is there anything I can do now?

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:45.020
Kogane-chan, I will bring Kaoruko back here.

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:49.520
So I want you to wait 
here until I come back.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:53.400
All right.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:56.220
Thanks, Kogane-chan.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:58.190
Be careful, A-chan.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:18:58.780
Okay.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.440
I'll be back soon.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:14.670
Yes. Then we will begin the execution now.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.900
What? What is all this?

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.680
What are you gonna do?!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.360
You pervert! Freak!

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:25.940
Release me! Release me right now!

00:19:27.320 --> 00:19:29.300
Damn it, these are tight!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.730
Come on, you stupid...

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.650
Double?

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:38.570
You're gonna kill me?!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.270
But you told me to get in Entei 
and kill all those people!

00:19:42.270 --> 00:19:44.250
Was that a lie, too?

00:19:44.250 --> 00:19:46.620
Why does everyone keep lying to me?

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:49.560
I'm sick of being lied to all the time.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:53.240
I'm sick of having no one care about me!

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:56.310
Mom... Dad...

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:57.500
Help me!

00:20:00.440 --> 00:20:02.630
No! No! I don't wanna die!

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.240
I haven't done anything yet!

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:09.560
I want to travel the world, fall in love, 
have a boyfriend, and get married!

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:13.310
I don't want to die!

00:20:21.310 --> 00:20:25.950
It's good to cry your eyes out once 
in a while, isn't it, Kaoruko-chan?

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:29.580
Double? What's the idea?

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:33.080
Double? Non, non!

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:41.760
My name is Hazama Zetsubi!

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:45.360
One of Reoko-sama's Four Gods!

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.550
It's been so long since I 
introduced myself that way.

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:49.970
Who in the world...?

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:53.600
I told you, I'm one of 
Reoko-sama's Four Gods.

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:56.980
I infiltrated Demokratia in 
the guise of a secretary

00:20:56.980 --> 00:21:00.860
to investigate Reoko-sama's 
bitter enemy, Guy!

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:04.070
I've basically gotten what I came for,

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.330
so now we're going to get out of here.

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:10.410
Sorry about this.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:14.280
I need your help for just a bit longer.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:26.590
Well, well! You're a strong one!

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:31.220
I'm alive right now!

00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:48.660
Pardon me, but I live in the area.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.740
There isn't much sightseeing to do here.

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:53.600
Where are you headed?

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:54.850
Well...

00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:58.010
I only know the general direction...

00:21:58.010 --> 00:21:59.210
I'll take you there.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.340
Get in.

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:03.210
Thank you!
